  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The legacy golf-course operations in Florida are under pressure, with declining rounds played eroding the viability of the core business and pushing the company into losses. This deterioration is the direct catalyst for a radical strategic pivot away from hospitality toward an entirely different industry with different demand drivers, regulatory backstops, and competitive dynamics.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is orchestrating a reverse-merger with Autonomous Power Corp. to transform the failing golf micro-cap into an NDAA-compliant counter‑drone manufacturer. The move is framed as an asymmetric bet where success hinges entirely on closing the deal, then executing in a complex defense supply chain — a path that introduces significant dilution risk and shifts the investment case from asset liquidation to start‑up scaling.",
